//
// Public API of the known-param table (declarations only; the data lives in the .cpp).
//
// The problem it solves: a `TryGet*Field` that fails returns the default SILENTLY,
// in every command, so a typo in a param key reads exactly like "that option did
// nothing" (sending the params at the root level instead of inside params:{} once
// killed the editor). This table is what makes it possible to ANSWER "nobody reads
// that key" instead of swallowing it.
//
// It is NOT a validator: the dispatcher REPORTS the finding (data.unknown_params)
// and runs the command anyway. Rejecting would break existing callers.
//
// Coverage: 2097 commands / 6431 param names.
